{
 "title": "Bayesian Parametric Portfolio Policies",
 "hypothesis": "Factor timing as portfolio rule. BPPP (posterior-averaged conditional PPP with 242 predictors -> 5 factors) earns timing component vs static and survives leverage limit and turnover penalty.",
 "data_sources": [
  "Kenneth French data library: monthly market total return Mkt, SMB, HML, CMA, RMW, UMD zero-investment factor returns, 1-month T-bill",
  "Open Source Asset Pricing: 212 monthly anomaly portfolio returns (aggregate, same for every factor)",
  "30 factor-specific predictors: time-series momentum, cross-sectional momentum, valuation on past prices, reversal, volatility computed from own factor returns (6 series x 5 families, Appendix A)"
 ],
 "sample": "Monthly factor returns. Full sample July 1963 to December 2023. Burn-in 121 months used only for estimation. Rolling estimation window 120 months. OOS evaluation August 1973 to December 2023 = 605 months. All predictors standardised using only data available at date, winsorized at 3 SD, missing=0, first 12 expanding-standardisation rows =0. z_t = [constant + 242 standardised predictors], L=243, K=5 factors, K*L=1,215 coefficients. Market weight fixed 1, benchmark factor weights 0. Position limit c=0.6 per factor, gross limit g=1.5, applied after capping via proportional scaling if sum|w|>g. Factors zero-investment, no budget constraint linking to market. Net returns deduct factor-specific trading costs and holding costs at factor level, market not costed, no netting across factors. Historical data vintages not reconstructed.",
 "period_start": "July 1963",
 "period_end": "December 2023",
 "method": [
  "1. Predictors: compute 212 aggregate anomaly returns + 30 factor-specific signals as defined in Appendix A. Standardise each predictor with expanding mean/SD to current date, winsorise at 3 SD, set missing to 0. First complete look-back missing retained. At startup first 12 rows after expanding standardisation left at 0. Append constant => L=NSignalsPolicy=243. Policy size NCoefficientsPolicy=1,215.",
  "2. Policy: w_{m,t}=1, w_{k,t}(theta)=Pi_c(theta_k' z_t) for k=1..5, Pi_c(u)=min(c,max(-c,u)), c=TimingCap=0.6. Feasible set W={(1,w): |w_k|<=c, sum|w_k|<=g}, g=TimingLeverage=1.5. Portfolio return r_{p,t+1}=r_{m,t+1}+ w_t' F_{t+1}. Estimation criterion on window T_t of 120 months: f(theta)= -omega sum_{s in T_t} U(q_s(theta)) + 0.5 theta' Lambda theta, U(q)=(q^{1-gamma}-1)/(1-gamma), gamma=RiskAversion=5, q_s(theta)=1+r_{m,s+1}+ sum_k theta_k' z_s F_{k,s+1} linear in theta (affine surrogate, limits not inside q). Prior Gaussian theta_{k,l}~N(0,lambda_l^{-1}), lambda_0=delta_s^{-2} delta_s=0.8, lambda_{l>=1}=(L-1) delta_tau^{-2} delta_tau=1 (prior of BrandtSantaClara 2006 III.B). Lambda diagonal precision.",
  "3. Learning rate omega: diagonal covariance-trace matching heuristic using empirical diagonals of H and V with Bartlett weights, median TimingOmega=5.80. Compute provisional mode at provisional omega, evaluate omega-hat_t = sum_{j in I} H_{jj}^{-1} / sum_{j in I} V_{jj} H_{jj}^{-2}, I={j: H_{jj}>xi} xi very small, recompute mode at omega-hat_t. One-pass, not fixed point. Full inverse does not exist (rank<=T). Motivation distinct from Lyddon et al 2019.",
  "4. Optimisation: exploit kernel K_{ss'}=(F_{s+1}'F_{s'+1})(z_s' Lambda_L^{-1} z_{s'}), Lambda_L=diag(lambda_l), wealth q=1+r_m+K alpha, theta=Lambda^{-1} sum_s alpha_s G_s. Solve rho(alpha)=alpha - omega q(alpha)^{-gamma}=0 by Newton from 0 with backtracking. Strongly convex => unique mode. Bound f(theta)-min f <=0.5 rho' K rho <=0.5 grad' Lambda^{-1} grad (Lemma 1). Accept only when bound sufficiently small including provisional and bootstrap fits.",
  "5. Posterior averaging (BPPP) vs mode (RPPP): Laplace approximation posterior N(hat_theta_t, C_t). Unconstrained weight X=theta_k' z_t ~ N(mu_k, sigma_k^2), mu_k=hat_theta_k' z_t, sigma_k^2=z_t' C_{kk} z_t via Woodbury sigma_k^2= z'Lambda_L^{-1}z - h_k'(D^{-1}+K)^{-1}h_k, D=omega gamma diag(q^{-gamma-1}), h_{k,s}=F_{k,s+1}(z_s' Lambda_L^{-1}z_t). Averaged constrained weight E[Pi_c(X)] closed form -c Phi(a)+mu[Phi(b)-Phi(a)]+sigma[phi(a)-phi(b)]+c[1-Phi(b)], a=(-c-mu)/sigma, b=(c-mu)/sigma. Then gross scaling. RPPP weight Pi_c(mu_k) then same gross scaling. Prior scales and omega same for BPPP/RPPP, only averaging differs.",
  "6. Exact posterior check: likelihood depends only through u=G theta in R^T, u~N(0,K) prior, posterior of u proportional to N(u;0,K) exp{omega sum U(1+r_m+u)} on positive wealth, rank(K)<=T (first 7 windows rank 113-119, min retained RevExactMinRank=113). Conditional X_k|u normal. Estimate E_u[closed form] by HMC preconditioned at mode (32 chains, 300 burn-in, 700 retained, 12 steps size 0.3 whitened, 12 date shards seeds 1-12, median acceptance RevExactAccept=95%, max Rhat RevExactRhatMax=1.005, median/max MCSE RevExactMcseMedian=0.0037 RevExactMcseMax=0.0014 with Bartlett 100 lags).",
  "7. Comparators, same limits c=0.6 g=1.5 unless noted: constant allocation maximises CRRA net of holding costs over all past returns subject to both limits; minimum variance minimises variance of whole portfolio using past 120m covariance; scaled min-var rescales to gross bound minimising variance; inverse variance and reward-to-risk proportional to inverse variance or positive mean/variance past 60m; lasso regresses vector of ones on past 120m factor returns (BrittenJones 1999 tangency) penalty by hold-out Sharpe, scaled to vol target; conditional mean-variance ridge forecasts each factor via ridge on same 242 predictors averaged over past 12 or 48m, then mean-variance with gamma=5, penalty and window chosen every 24m by past CE.",
  "8. Timing decomposition: E[w_{k,t}F_{k,t+1}]=E[w]E[F]+Cov(w,F) (Lo 2008) summed over 5 factors, divisor T. Active return vs market = static + timing. Exposure = average sum|w|. Turnover =12 * average monthly sum_k|w_{k,t}-w_{k,t-1}|. Gross CE =12[ {T^{-1} sum(1+r_p)^{1-gamma}}^{1/(1-gamma)}-1], Sharpe= sqrt(12) mean(r_p)/sd(r_p), excess subtracts bill. HAC Newey-West Bartlett bandwidth floor(4(T/100)^{2/9})=5 at full sample. Paired Sharpe difference delta-method HAC LedoitWolf 2008 Sec 3.1 with Holm correction. Net returns: r^n_{t+1}=r_{m}+w'F - sum phi_k|delta w_k| - sum h_k|w_k|, phi =60,25,30,30,70 bps trading (SMB,HML,CMA,RMW,UMD), h=90,40,45,45,80 bps annual holding charged monthly, market not costed, initial purchase not charged.",
  "9. Turnover penalty: f_kappa(theta)=f(theta)+ omega*kappa/2 sum_{s>min T_t} sum_k phi_k[theta_k'(z_s - z_{s-1})]^2, kappa>=0 quadratic proxy = linear cost at monthly raw change 2/kappa, depends only on within-window consecutive pairs T-1, adds omega kappa phi_k dZ'dZ to prior precision block A_k=Lambda_L+omega kappa phi_k dZ'dZ, K=sum_k(F_kF_k') circ (Z A_k^{-1} Z'), learning rate calibrated without penalty and held fixed. Penalty falls only on timing coefficients (constant unchanged).",
  "10. Bagged ridge: 100 circular block-bootstrap samples of window block 12m, re-estimate mode same prior/omega, constrain to [-c,c], average constrained weights then gross scale. Tighter prior variants multiply both delta_s,delta_tau by 0.4-0.9 or timing-only scales 0.5,0.2. Constant scaling of RPPP by a in [0.05,1] before limits for frontier. Recursive prior/ kappa selection: grid {0.4,0.8,1.6}x{0.5,1.0,1.5} and 3x3x3 for kappa, chosen each month by highest past OOS CE (first 36m centre of grid, turnover includes spec change), net CE for cost section.",
  "11. Costs: null hypotheses timing=0, Sharpe difference=0. Where paper does not state, write not stated. Theoretical Sharpe benchmark not stated. Return prediction not modelled in PPP (generalised posterior Bissiri 2016). Predictor set assembled ex post; publication-lagged check uses each anomaly from publication year (+2y lag) and restricts post-2000 analysis when all public."
 ],
